title: Graduation_Start
tags:
---
<<wait_for_action meet_maya_at_gate>>
maya-didi: Come here. Stand at the gate. Look across the road.
<<wait_for_action look_at_bank_bazaar>>
maya-didi: The building with the blue sign — the Still Pool.
maya-didi: One month, you have been a First Dojo apprentice. Envelopes. Jars. Lists.
maya-didi: Now you are ready for a teller window.
<<player_choose>>
-> "I'm not sure I'm ready."
    maya-didi: You paid rent on time. You said no to knockoff buds.
    maya-didi: You counted seven days of tea. You locked a jar.
    maya-didi: You are exactly ready. Trust the work you already did.
    <<jump Graduation_Handoff>>
-> "Why a bank? Envelopes work."
    maya-didi: Envelopes don't earn interest. Envelopes can be stolen.
    maya-didi: The Still Pool will show you an account, a Term Vault, a tap-pay.
    maya-didi: Same idea — envelopes — with locks made of law.
    <<jump Graduation_Handoff>>
-> "Walk with me, sensei."
    maya-didi: I'll walk you to the door. Inside, you're on your own.
    <<jump Graduation_Handoff>>
===

title: Graduation_Handoff
tags:
---
maya-didi: One last thing. Take this notebook. Everything we did is in it.
<<wait_for_action receive_chawl_notebook>>
maya-didi: Income minus expenses. Needs vs wants. Rent first. Small leaks.
maya-didi: The emergency jar. Five lessons. Carry them across the road.
<<player_choose>>
-> "Thank you, sensei."
    maya-didi: Enough. Don't be sentimental. Go.
    <<set_flag thanked_maya>>
-> "Will I see you again?"
    maya-didi: Of course. The First Dojo is your home. I am at envelope number one.
    <<set_flag will_visit_maya>>
<<continue>>
<<grant_inr 50>>
maya-didi: Fifty. Opening balance. Don't put it in a jar. Put it in an account.
<<grant_mastery budgeting.graduation 1>>
<<unlock_district bank-bazaar>>
<<set_flag finished_chawl_mohalla>>
maya-didi: Go. The Still Pool is waiting. And so is the rest of the city.
===
